    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio",
    "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $3$ and the common ratio is $15?$",
    "worked_solution": "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=15.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{15}^{N})}{1-15} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{14}(1-{15}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
